    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2003-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The units digit of \\(13^{2003}\\) matches that of \\(3^{2003}.\\)\n\nPowers of \\(3\\) have units digits cycling \\(3,\\) \\(9,\\) \\(7,\\) \\(1\\) with period \\(4.\\)\n\nSince \\(2003 = 4 \\cdot 500 + 3,\\) the units digit is the third in the cycle, which is \\(7.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "The units digit of \\(13^n\\) equals the units digit of \\(3^n\\)",
        "Units digits of powers of \\(3\\) cycle \\(3,\\) \\(9,\\) \\(7,\\) \\(1\\) with period \\(4\\)"
      ],
